WEBVTT

NOTE English descriptive captions for the silent FlashLearn PWD demo video (an 81-second tour recorded on a tablet).

00:00.000 --> 00:04.400
We open FlashLearn PWD and choose a profile — no login or email needed.

00:04.400 --> 00:10.000
Home shows the learner's streak, words learned and stars, then My Day and a mood check-in.

00:10.000 --> 00:12.800
One tap records how they feel today.

00:12.800 --> 00:17.300
The Daily Challenge asks what “Sit” is in Filipino. “Umupo” — correct, with bonus stars!

00:17.300 --> 00:20.600
Cards opens the flashcard decks, grouped by topic.

00:20.600 --> 00:23.700
Each card shows a picture with the English and Filipino word: Dog — Aso.

00:23.700 --> 00:26.500
Flipping the card shows details and an example sentence.

00:26.500 --> 00:31.500
The FSL button plays a Filipino Sign Language video of the word…

00:31.500 --> 00:37.900
…with Replay and speed controls, so learners can practise at their own pace.

00:37.900 --> 00:46.300
In Games, “Auto” suggests a difficulty based on the learner's recent accuracy.

00:46.300 --> 00:49.500
Next, we pick which word categories to practise…

00:49.500 --> 01:00.300
…and play! Word Match asks for the English word for each Filipino word and picture.

01:00.300 --> 01:06.300
Further down, Home has many more activities: learning paths, guided practice, assessments, the FSL Dictionary and more.

01:06.300 --> 01:14.200
The Talk Board helps learners communicate: tap picture tiles to build a sentence, then hear it read aloud.

01:14.200 --> 01:17.000
One tap switches the board to Filipino: “Kamusta. Nauuhaw ako.”

01:17.000 --> 01:21.500
Progress shows the streak, stars, words learned, level and overall mastery.
